{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"depraved-classless-rooster","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nAfter `forcible-diminished-lamb` and `salmon-abominable-pupa`, both review pipelines have Terraform-scoped tool sessions [rebar:salmon-abominable-pupa]. This slice adds `probe_source` so agents can disprove a claim that a declared module/provider source is unavailable when the source is already local or its registry metadata is positively reachable. It never downloads module content and never treats failed access as nonexistence.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_source.py` and expose `probe_source(source, from_module)` through the established Terraform-only Pass-1 and Pass-2 sessions.\n\n### Local sources\n\n- Normalize Terraform's literal local source forms relative to `from_module`.\n- Return positive T1 structural evidence only when the resolved directory remains under the repository root, contains an indexable Terraform module, and is included in the bounded immutable closure.\n- An absolute path, an escaping `../`, an escaping symlink, an unreadable directory, a missing target, or a dynamic source returns ABSTAIN. Absence is never asserted.\n- Already-downloaded `.terraform/modules` content is excluded: it is generated, may be stale, and is not part of the client project's attested source snapshot.\n\n### Registry metadata\n\n- Recognize Terraform provider registry addresses and native module registry addresses, including an explicit hostname. Normalize omitted provider/module hostnames to Terraform's documented default.\n- Use Terraform Registry service discovery and version/metadata endpoints only. Accept a source as positive T0 evidence only after a bounded HTTPS response is successful, size-limited, and schema-valid. Do not follow or request any module download URL returned by metadata.\n- Permit the public default registry. For a custom host, permit a globally routable DNS target or an exact hostname trusted by an ambient Terraform credential entry. Reject embedded URL credentials, literal IP targets, non-HTTPS services, and cross-host redirects. A private-address custom host requires the exact credentialed hostname.\n- Bound metadata to 1 MiB per response and the existing 60-second grounding deadline. Use the existing fail-open HTTP seam/harness; no new HTTP dependency.\n- A 2xx schema-valid response yields only count/digest/source-kind facts, never response bodies or remote source contents.\n\n### Ambient credentials\n\nFollow Terraform's precedence and hostname normalization for:\n\n1. `TF_TOKEN_<hostname>` environment credentials.\n2. The static file selected by `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE`, else platform-default Terraform CLI config.\n3. Terraform's static `credentials.tfrc.json`.\n\nRead only literal `credentials` entries for the exact registry hostname. Never prompt, write a credential file, execute a `credentials_helper`, import cloud/provider credentials, or use credentials for another host. Output/receipts/logs identify only `auth_source=environment|static-file|none`; they contain no token, token hash, home path, header, or raw error body.\n\n### Error and outcome contract\n\n`probe_source` uses `job=refute`: a positive registry hit returns `refuted` at T0 and a positive local module returns `refuted` at T1, disproving asserted absence. Every other result is ABSTAIN:\n\n- 401/403/404 and private/ambiguous responses → `private_or_internal_suspected`.\n- 429 → `rate_limited`.\n- DNS/TLS/proxy/5xx/redirect rejection → `network_error`.\n- deadline → `timeout`.\n- malformed/oversized metadata → `parse_error`.\n- dynamic, unsupported, or non-registry remote source → `ambiguous`.\n\nNo arm emits an “absent”, “missing”, clean, or negative match.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nPositive-only metadata mirrors Rebar's existing package-existence oracle and preserves its asymmetric safety: reachable evidence can refute a weak LLM claim, while inaccessible evidence says nothing. Exact-host ambient credentials meet already-authenticated users where they are without adding Rebar auth configuration.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRemote module downloads/fetch, Git/HTTP/S3/GCS source checkout, Terraform Cloud API operations beyond registry discovery, credential helpers, new auth configuration, provider/cloud credentials, and all Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution. The ADR must state that ambient-credential remote content fetch is approved as a future feature if demand justifies the additional containment; it is not implemented in V1.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Local-source tests return positive T1 evidence for a literal repo-contained child and ABSTAIN for missing, absolute, escaping, symlink-escaping, unreadable, generated-cache, and dynamic sources without exposing partial facts.\n- [ ] Registry protocol tests return positive T0 evidence only for successful schema-valid provider/module metadata and assert that no download URL or module archive endpoint is requested.\n- [ ] Credential-precedence tests cover Terraform hostname encoding, environment-over-static precedence, `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE`, platform defaults, and `credentials.tfrc.json`; helper blocks are ignored and no credential value/hash/path appears in results, receipts, logs, or raised test diagnostics.\n- [ ] The access matrix maps 401/403/404, 429, DNS, TLS, proxy, 5xx, rejected redirect, timeout, malformed JSON, and oversized response to the specified closed abstention and never to nonexistence.\n- [ ] Network-target tests allow the public default registry, a globally routable custom registry, and an exact credentialed private hostname while rejecting HTTP, embedded credentials, literal IPs, uncredentialed private targets, and cross-host redirects before sending a token.\n- [ ] Plan-review T10 and code-review IaC Pass 1/Pass 2 advertise `probe_source` with the two prerequisite operations; non-Terraform steps and missing-extra runs advertise none.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md` and `docs/grounding.md` distinguish V1 metadata probing from prohibited remote fetch and record future ambient-credential fetch as approved-but-deferred.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, Terraform's registry/CLI-credential protocols, and the prerequisite tool-session contract [rebar:salmon-abominable-pupa].\n- Preconditions: temp repo local modules plus a stateful registry fake serving valid, auth-required, error, redirect, oversized, and download-advertising responses.\n- Production path: real source normalization/credential selection/HTTP response parser through the tool; only DNS/socket transport is faked.\n- Tiers: unit tests for paths/credentials; stateful external-service contract tests for registry mapping; workflow integration for tool visibility.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/tier/reason and requested endpoint/headers, with byte scans proving the secret and download URL never escape or get fetched.\n- Negative controls: a valid public hit refutes absence; the nearest 404 and authenticated access denial both abstain.\n- CI: `make test`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`","id":"1c52-5e73-4d61-4124","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","priority":3,"tags":["terraform","grounding","registry","credentials","optional"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Probe local and registry Terraform sources with ambient access"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788469697004204527,"uuid":"960e49fd-984a-4f49-bfbd-fac38f49afc1"}